  "guard": "orch tool guard",
  "note": "One decision table for both harness guards. rule is the rule that must block the call, or empty when the call is allowed. situation names the PATH the hook runs with: orch on PATH, orch on PATH but broken (a stub that exits 1), no orch but fd and rg installed, or neither. A situation's optional broken list names the tools whose stub exits 1 instead of 0. hooks/claude/toolguard_test.py runs every case through the real Claude hooks; TestCtxReminderSharedToolguardCases in tool runs the same file through the pi extension and compares blocked vs allowed and the rule name only. builtinCases is the second table: the built-in search tools, where tool names and rule ids differ by harness, so it names a harness-neutral tool (content-search for pi grep and Claude Grep, file-search for pi find and Claude Glob) and the rule each harness must block with (empty for allowed). path names the target directory; an absolute path outside the repository must be allowed, because orch ctx is pinned to a git repository root and has no answer there.",
  "pathSituations": {
